cff-version: 1.2.0
title: eyeprocesspy
message: "If you use eyeprocesspy, cite the archived software release DOI and report both the eyeprocesspy version and frozen R reference version."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Balaskas
    given-names: Stefanos
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2444-9796
version: 0.2.2
date-released: 2026-09-27
repository-code: https://github.com/stefanosbalaskas/eyeprocesspy
url: https://stefanosbalaskas.github.io/eyeprocesspy/
license: MIT
keywords:
  - eye-tracking
  - pupillometry
  - biometrics
  - psychometrics
  - item response theory
  - multimodal process data
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  eyeprocesspy is vendor-neutral Python infrastructure for harmonizing,
  validating, processing, analysing, and documenting eye-tracking,
  pupillometry, biometric, psychometric, and multimodal process data. Version
  0.2.2 extends the complete frozen R eyeprocess 0.11.1 parity foundation with
  measurement-validity and dynamic-gaze capabilities, including target-referenced
  spatial-error and pupil-size artefact correction, dynamic AOIs, pursuit and
  microsaccade analysis, event-detector benchmarking, naturalistic coordinates,
  scanpath metric sensitivity, eye-tracking stress testing, and a completed
  Bayesian-network robustness layer, while preserving explicit scientific
  interpretation boundaries and exact release qualification.
